orchestrator_stranded.body:
The orchestrator{series, select, none {} other { of series `{series}`}} runs on `{backend}`, which is {cause, select, quota {out of quota} auth {sidelined after an authentication failure} other {sidelined by the circuit breaker}}. Its declared fallback, the other {provider} connections it may use, the equivalent models and the global fallback are all unavailable: it stays stopped, and the returns of its tasks wait.

**Action needed** (one is enough):
- sign in another {provider} account, or another provider, among the subscription accounts of the settings;
- give the orchestrator a fallback that works: `timon series fallback set{seriesFlag} --scope orchestrator --backend <backend> --model <model>`;
- or wait: it can resume once `{backend}` is back ({until, date, medium} {until, time, short}).

backend_breaker_tripped.body:
`{backend}` has returned {failures} mission(s) in a row without producing a single turn ({signature}), inside {seconds} s.

**The cause is unknown** — no usable error message. This signature matches a broken login, an account with no credit, or a dead endpoint. Worth checking the backend CLI by hand.{minutes, plural, =0 {} other {

This backend has not completed a single turn since the daemon started, so a setup problem is the likeliest cause (login, CLI version, binary not found). It is sidelined for # min only: fix, then send the message again.}}

- Backend sidelined until {until, date, medium} {until, time, short}, or until a turn succeeds on it.
- Missions and tasks that depend on it switch onto their fallback plan.
